---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import {published,guides,states,origins,markets,rules,sources,topicNames,statusLabel,sourceById} from '../lib/content';
const us=states.filter(s=>s.kind!=='territory'); const territories=states.filter(s=>s.kind==='territory');
const candidates=(await import('../data/page-candidates.json').catch(()=>({default:[]}))).default;
const verified=rules.filter(r=>r.status==='verified').length;
---
<Base title="Research coverage, source status and unresolved work" action="Build our U.S. plan"><section class="container"><div class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE, WITH ITS BOUNDARIES</span><h1>Know what’s covered.<br/>See what isn’t.</h1><p class="lede">A franchise-law finding does not establish tax, employment or local operating clearance. This register tracks each topic separately and keeps missing research visible.</p></div><div class="metrics"><div class="metric"><strong>{published.length}</strong><span>Published canonical guides</span></div><div class="metric"><strong>{verified}</strong><span>Verified rule records · AI-assisted review</span></div><div class="metric"><strong>{us.length}</strong><span>State/DC coverage records</span></div><div class="metric"><strong>{markets.length}</strong><span>Named municipal market records</span></div></div><p class="scope-note">This is an initial publication batch. “Verified” means the recorded general explanation was checked against the cited source in this batch. It does not mean a transaction is cleared, all current law is covered, or a professional reviewer approved the material. <a href="/methodology/">Read the method</a>.</p><nav class="filter-list" aria-label="Coverage sections"><a href="#national">States & D.C.</a><a href="#territories">Territories</a><a href="#origins">Origin countries</a><a href="#local">Local markets</a><a href="#editorial">Publication inventory</a><a href="/sources/">Source register</a></nav><section id="national" class="anchor-section"><h2>The national register</h2><p>All 50 states and Washington, D.C. have records. Each franchise dimension below is independent. A source not yet checked is “not researched,” including in states without a researched filing requirement.</p><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="State and District topic coverage"><table class="coverage-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Jurisdiction</th>{Object.values(topicNames).map(t=><th scope="col">{t}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{us.map(s=><tr><th scope="row"><a href={'#state-'+s.slug}>{s.name}</a></th>{Object.keys(topicNames).map(t=><td><span class:list={['pill',statusLabel(s.topics?.[t]).replaceAll(' ','-')]}>{statusLabel(s.topics?.[t])}</span></td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div>{us.map(s=><details id={'state-'+s.slug}><summary>{s.name} — franchise dimensions</summary><div>{s.franchise?<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Source-backed status & scope</th></tr></thead><tbody>{['registration','notice','exemptions','disclosure','advertising','relationship'].map(k=>{const d=s.franchise[k];return <tr><th scope="row">{k}</th><td><span class="pill">{statusLabel(d)}</span><p>{typeof d==='object'?d?.summary:d}</p>{d?.sourceIds?.map((id:string)=>{const source=sourceById(id);return source?<a href={source.url}>{source.title} </a>:null})}</td></tr>})}</tbody></table></div>:<p>No franchise dimensions researched yet.</p>}<p class="meta">{s.notes}</p>{s.franchise?.limitations?.map((l:string)=><p class="meta">{l}</p>)}{published.filter(g=>g.jurisdictions?.some((j:string)=>[s.id,s.name,s.slug].includes(j))).map(g=><p><a href={g.path}>{g.title}</a></p>)}</div></details>)}</section><section id="territories" class="sources anchor-section"><h2>A separate territorial workstream</h2><p>Puerto Rico, the U.S. Virgin Islands, Guam, the Northern Mariana Islands and American Samoa have separate records. Mainland assumptions do not establish their franchise, tax, immigration, import or operating rules.</p>{territories.map(t=><details><summary>{t.name} <span class="pill">{statusLabel(t.topics?.classification)}</span></summary><div><p>{t.notes}</p><div class="topic-grid">{Object.entries(topicNames).map(([key,name])=><div><span>{name}</span><span>{statusLabel(t.topics?.[key])}</span></div>)}</div></div></details>)}</section><section id="origins" class="sources anchor-section"><h2>Origin-country coverage</h2><p>All eleven Southeast Asian countries are registered. Europe follows a documented UN M49 geographic baseline, with separately identified supplementary and dependency records. EU membership, geography, incorporation and owners’ nationality are different facts.</p><p class="meta"><a href="/methodology/#geography">Read the geographic convention</a>. A country’s presence here does not establish a country-specific legal conclusion.</p>{origins.map(o=><details><summary>{o.name} <span class="meta">{o.convention??o.region??''}</span></summary><div><p>{o.notes}</p><div class="topic-grid">{Object.entries(topicNames).map(([key,name])=><div><span>{name}</span><span>{statusLabel(o.topics?.[key])}</span></div>)}</div>{(o.sourceIds??[]).map((id:string)=>{const s=sourceById(id);return s?<p><a href={s.url}>{s.title}</a></p>:null})}</div></details>)}</section><section id="local" class="sources anchor-section"><h2>Markets, with actual boundaries</h2><p>These markets were selected for varied business contexts and accessible primary sources. They are research starting points, not a ranking of the best places to expand. A narrow municipal process check does not establish full local coverage.</p>{markets.map(m=><details><summary>{m.name} <span class="meta">{m.state} · {m.status}</span></summary><div><p><strong>Municipality:</strong> {m.municipality}. <strong>County:</strong> {m.county}. <strong>Boundary:</strong> {m.boundary}</p><p class="meta">Commercial region: {m.commercialRegion} — a comparison label, not a lawmaking jurisdiction.</p>{m.processes?.map((p:any)=><div class="source-record"><h3>{p.title}</h3><p>{p.summary}</p><p><strong>Trigger:</strong> {p.trigger}. <strong>Authority:</strong> {p.authority}. <span class="pill">{p.status}</span></p><a href={p.url}>Primary process source</a></div>)}<h3>Still unresolved</h3><ul>{m.unresolved?.map((u:string)=><li>{u}</li>)}</ul></div></details>)}</section><section id="editorial" class="sources anchor-section"><h2>The publication inventory</h2><p>{candidates.length} candidate page records are editorial research targets. They are not counted as published guides and do not generate public article routes. Every candidate must earn publication through distinct evidence, applicability review and a practical output.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Content status</th><th>Guide records</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Published</td><td>{published.length}</td><td>Canonical substantive pages built into public HTML.</td></tr><tr><td>Reviewed</td><td>{guides.filter(g=>g.lastReviewed&&g.reviewStatus).length}</td><td>Guide records with a dated AI-assisted review. May overlap published.</td></tr><tr><td>Draft</td><td>{guides.filter(g=>g.status==='draft').length}</td><td>Not built as public article routes.</td></tr><tr><td>Blocked</td><td>{guides.filter(g=>g.status==='blocked').length}</td><td>Material access, evidence or conflict dependency remains.</td></tr><tr><td>Not researched</td><td>{candidates.filter((c:any)=>!published.some(g=>g.path===c.path)&&['not-researched','unresearched','candidate'].includes(c.status)).length}</td><td>Outstanding candidate paths after excluding matches to published guides.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="meta">{sources.length} source records · {rules.length} canonical rules. <a href="/sources/">Inspect source-to-page dependencies</a>.</p></section></section></Base>
